  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As it was predicted, group instances are a blessing and a curse. On one hand, public instances can now be moderated. On the other hand, abuse of power and unfair treatment. Currently Groups can block you and you can no longer join their public instance. And the worst part is that even if you are a World Author of a Group Public Instance, you can be booted from your own world and treated unfairly as well. \n\nSo, if Groups can block people, shouldn't people be able to block Groups as well? \n\nBlocking the Group would disallow a Group to create either all Group or at least Group Public instances.\n\nP.S. Ideally, a World Author should have the ultimate power over their world, but being able to block Groups and therefore disllowing them to create Group Public instances would be sufficient.",
